rsified Retail NBFC / Vehicle + MSME + Gold Finance","tag":"General","theme":"Auto & Mobility","tier":""}],"thesis":"A very strong, capital-flush quarter: PAT +59.8% to INR3,444.56cr, NII +33.7% to INR8,055.70cr and NIM at a peak 9.04%  — turbo-charged by the ~INR39,600cr equity infusion (April 2026) that added ~INR500cr of NII, cut leverage to 2.14x (from 3.82x) and lifted CAR to 34.1%. Disbursements +19.5% and AUM +15.3% YoY  on a GST-cut-driven auto up-cycle, with used/new-CV demand resilient despite the West-Asia war. Management reaffirms an **18% FY27 growth** guide , a medium-term normalisation of NIM to ~8.5% as new-vehicle mix rises, ~2% credit-cost, and outsized gold/MSME expansion. Asset quality stable . The one debate: whether the ~9% NIM can be held vs management's deliberately conservative 8.5% medium-term guide.","trig":[]},"lm":"2025-12","m":263282,"mem":0,"pdd":"2024-06-20","prev_stage":2,"prev_zone_vpe":1.1,"r":99.1,"s":"SHRIRAMFIN","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"1059.5","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"3.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"0.0","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":""}},"s":"SHRIRAMFIN"}